The heights is a list of 7, 4, 7, 5, 6, and 5.
The ranks is a list of 0, 4, 1, 0, 1, and 2.
The last is the last position of heights.
For every left from 0 to last.
For every right from left plus 1 to last.
The taller is 0.
If item right of heights is more than item left of heights, set taller to 1.
If item right of heights is item left of heights and item right of ranks is less than item left of ranks, set taller to 1.
If taller is 1, swap item left of heights and item right of heights, swap item left of ranks and item right of ranks.

